think My lane's own door is Keaton-gated: weave merge and annotate both landed with witnesses and controls, and the one seam left -- the several-line interleave wanting an anchor per insert -- stands under Still yours on the card. So the lane queue is empty and claim-as-override applies.
think Claimed from the %568 cadence set: dated_spelling, one of the five guards that first cadence sing found red. Read the two sites rather than the count, which is the habit %567 taught me one row ago.
think Both sites were shell case statements with TWO arms -- the sprigged spelling on one line, the sprigless on the next -- and both answered correctly. The meter greps line by line, so it saw the first arm alone and called it a pattern requiring the sprig.
think The repair was already written in the meter's own header: spell the separator as the class [_.]. One arm spelled that way matches exactly what the two arms matched, has no sibling to drift from, and is wholly visible to a line-reading grep. Neither the scans nor the meter needed widening.
think One site WAS narrow, pointing the other way: reds_citation's sprigless arm named .md alone, so a sprigless .kyri log read as living where the law calls it testimony. The one-arm form fixes that in the same character.
obs A red guard withholds the roster receipt, so --scoped refuses and eight ships pay a full cold pass. This red cost the whole pier for a defect that was not there.
obs Widening reds_citation moved nothing today -- its ten readings are unchanged field for field -- so the repair is honest about costing nothing now and holding for the first sprigless non-.md citer.
obs I named the blindness in the meter's own WHAT THIS DOES NOT REACH, which already named the blindness pointing the other way. A section that says what a guard cannot see should say it in both directions.
obs The cold open caught a peer's broken living link on the shared card -- archive/REDS-a-label-is-not-its-target-rows-571.md where the shelf is rows-570. One character, repaired here, since readme_reach reds in my tree for work landed in theirs.
rota lap 4188, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; the Happy Zone seat asks whether tests press on the design, and tasting these two scans up close rather than reading the meter's count is what found that the count was right and its subject was wrong.
loom scan=dated_spelling_scan files_considered=5257 narrow_before=2 narrow_after=0
